    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The Japanese expression '寡人' (かじん) is an archaic and humble first-person pronoun used historically by kings or emperors. It is not a general-purpose first-person pronoun and is completely unnatural and misleading for a modern language learner trying to express the concept of 'I' or 'me'. The English lemma 'i' (as a noun, referring to the self) represents a fundamental concept, for which '寡人' is a semantically incorrect and contextually inappropriate match.",
